        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>One of the first things that Tachyon did when designing Freedom tower was to ensure chronal and dimensional stability, so that the team would have a reliable base of operations. &nbsp;Temporal/Spatial Stability was attained by doping the construction materials with nanocamera protointelligences, ensuring that the entire building is always observed on a Quantum level, locking it into the moment and location. &nbsp;Magical/Dimensional stability is maintained through Tillinghast resonators in key locations and a greater Elder Sign inscribed around the periphery of the building. &nbsp;While none of this is perfect, they combine quite effectively and give the team a place to plan (or regroup, if necessary).</p><p>The final wasteland is not represented because it represents a future that is so far along the causality gradient that small temporal events don&#39;t have the necessary energy to punch through the likeliness barrier. &nbsp;Most of the events in the Time cataclysm are clustered around events the Freedom 5 have personally observed, which substantially lowers the chronal energy necessary to get to them. &nbsp;1883 requires an even higher energy cost, given that it is farther back, thus the efforts to sustain the portal and get back before it collapses. &nbsp;Getting to the final wasteland is even more difficult, and requires special equipment (such as Jim&#39;s badge), a highly energetic time rift, or taking the long road (Haka).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
