        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/danmarshall14/{size}/1944_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-02T15:16:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"jmrburgard\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/9fc29f/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jmrburgard:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Has anyone else tried opening a time rift in the middle of the game?&nbsp;The way I do it is take Rift in Time from Time Cataclysm (or a portal card from Silver Gulch) and put shuffle it face up into another environment deck (say Megalopolis). When it is revealed all the current environment cards are removed from play (rather than letting Dominion or Akash'bhuta feed of them) and the new environment deck (Time Cataclysm or Silver Gulch) is put into play. Basically the heroes and the villian get pulled randomly through time.&nbsp;I haven't thought up any other decks to do this with, but it provides a nice versatility to the environments (which I wish there was more of. How about a mini-expansion with 4 environments?). You never know when you'll suddenly be dealing with a sudden triceretops instead of falling gargoyles.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>That's an interesting idea.&nbsp; I've changed up games a little by giving heroes a \"home court advantage\" when fighting in their respective environments.&nbsp; For instance, Ra can heal 1 HP/turn (as well as Anubis/Ennead) if we're fighting in the Tomb of Anubis.&nbsp; Chrono Ranger deals an extra damage to the outlaws in Silver Gulch.&nbsp; La Capitan and Omnitron-X deal an extra damage when fighting in Time Cataclysm.&nbsp; The Wraith deals an extra damage to thugs in Rook City.&nbsp; And so on.&nbsp; It adds a little thematic fun to the matches.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>And I agree, I'd love to get an expansion of just environments.&nbsp; I was a little disappointed that there will only be 2 environments in Vengeance (as cool as they'll likely be)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:11.302Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
